{"task_id": "lcbv6__abc398_d", "arm": "solo__st_opus", "cap": "unit_code", "score": 1.0, "status": "ok", "answer": "Looking at this problem: a smoke particle born at time `b` sits at (0,0) at time `b+0.5`, then moves with the wind. Its position at time `t+0.5` is `P_t - P_b` where `P_t` is the cumulative wind displacement.\n\nA new particle is born at step `b` iff (0,0) is empty after the wind \u2014 which turns out to hold exactly when `P_b` is a *first occurrence* among `P_0..P_{b-1}`. So the set of \"reference points\" `{P_b : b born, b<=t}` equals the set of distinct prefix positions `{P_0,...,P_t}`.\n\nThus (R,C) is occupied at `t+0.5` iff `P_t - (R,C)` appears among `{P_0,...,P_t}`.\n\n```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.buffer.read().split()\n    n = int(data[0]); R = int(data[1]); C = int(data[2])\n    s = data[3].decode()\n\n    move = {\n        'N': (-1, 0),\n        'S': (1, 0),\n        'W': (0, -1),\n        'E': (0, 1),\n    }\n\n    seen = set()\n    r = c = 0\n    seen.add((0, 0))          # P_0\n    out = []\n\n    for ch in s:\n        dr, dc = move[ch]\n        r += dr\n        c += dc\n        seen.add((r, c))       # P_t\n        # need P_t - (R,C) in {P_0..P_t}\n        if (r - R, c - C) in seen:\n            out.append('1')\n        else:\n            out.append('0')\n\n    sys.stdout.write(''.join(out) + '\\n')\n\nmain()\n```", "finish": "stop"}
